      "hints": [
        "Parameterise $P$ on $l$ and impose the required distance from the origin.",
        "Square $|\\overrightarrow{OP}|=\\sqrt{14}$ to obtain a quadratic in $\\lambda$.",
        "Solve for both parameter values and substitute each into the line equation."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express the general position vector of point $P$ on line $l$ in terms of $\\lambda$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{OP} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 - \\lambda \\\\ 2 + \\lambda \\\\ -1 + 2\\lambda \\end{pmatrix}$$",
        "Set the square of its magnitude equal to $(\\sqrt{14})^2 = 14$:\n$$(1 - \\lambda)^2 + (2 + \\lambda)^2 + (-1 + 2\\lambda)^2 = 14$$",
        "Expand all squared terms:\n$$(1 - 2\\lambda + \\lambda^2) + (4 + 4\\lambda + \\lambda^2) + (1 - 4\\lambda + 4\\lambda^2) = 14$$\n$$6\\lambda^2 - 2\\lambda + 6 = 14$$\n$$6\\lambda^2 - 2\\lambda - 8 = 0$$",
        "Divide by $2$ and factorise the quadratic:\n$$3\\lambda^2 - \\lambda - 4 = 0$$\n$$(3\\lambda - 4)(\\lambda + 1) = 0$$\nThis gives two values for $\\lambda$:\n$$\\lambda = -1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\lambda = \\dfrac{4}{3}$$",
        "Substitute $\\lambda = -1$ into $\\overrightarrow{OP}$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{OP} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 - (-1) \\\\ 2 + (-1) \\\\ -1 + 2(-1) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} = 2\\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} - 3\\mathbf{k}$$",
        "Substitute $\\lambda = \\dfrac{4}{3}$ into $\\overrightarrow{OP}$:\n$$\\overrightarrow{OP} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 - \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 2 + \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ -1 + \\frac{8}{3} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} \\end{pmatrix} = -\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{i} + \\dfrac{10}{3}\\mathbf{j} + \\dfrac{5}{3}\\mathbf{k}$$"
      ],
